Package: EpidemicTrajectoriesR
Type: Package
Title: Discrete-Time Individual-Level Epidemic Models from R, via Julia
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Arthur", "Newbury", email = "a.r.newbury@exeter.ac.uk",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Specify, fit and check discrete-time individual-level epidemic
    models from R. Model structure -- states, transitions, tracked aggregates,
    the observation process -- is declared with R objects, and the rate and
    observation functions are written in a restricted subset of R that is
    transpiled to Julia. The generated Julia drives 'EpidemicTrajectories.jl'
    (simulator, autodiff likelihood, iFFBS latent-trajectory sampler),
    'PracticalBayes.jl' (the Gibbs and latent-kernel machinery) and
    'PracticalEpiBayes.jl' (the conjugate kernels), so the latent trajectory is
    resampled once per Gibbs sweep rather than inside every gradient call. The
    generated source is a first-class artefact: it is inspectable, runs
    standalone, and is the on-ramp to writing the model in Julia directly.
